d "q-8559" :question/id #uuid "d166a54d-b12b-5548-b477-26b9a92e7cfc" :question/math-academy-id "q-8559" :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the exact solutions to the equation $\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-\\frac{7\\pi }{3})+\\sqrt{3}=0$ for $0\\le x<\\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-\\frac{7\\pi }{3})+\\sqrt{3}=0 \\\\  & \\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-\\frac{7\\pi }{3})=-\\sqrt{3} \\\\  & \\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-\\frac{7\\pi }{3})=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-\\frac{7\\pi }{3} & =-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the equation above for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =\\frac{7\\pi }{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi  \\\\ 2x & =\\frac{25\\pi }{12}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{25\\pi }{24}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2} \\\\ x & =\\frac{(12n+25)\\pi }{24}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain $0\\le x<\\pi .$\n\n- Setting $n=-2$ gives $x=\\frac{\\pi }{24}$\n\n- Setting $n=-1$ gives $x=\\frac{13\\pi }{24}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain $0\\le x<\\pi .$ So, the solutions are $x=\\frac{\\pi }{24},\\frac{13\\pi }{24}.$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{24}\\cdot \\frac{13\\pi }{24}=\\frac{13{\\pi }^{2}}{576}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-8559/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9eb12a99-5169-52f7-8830-5de0d2d854f6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-8559"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-65851/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "da2fe10a-31ba-5123-8e80-121216668f3d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65851/selection/8edf36f0d0c04b8e0e3f881a66fab0f1901a06368d5ca1f6d437f77714de6bc5" :answer/id #uuid "ee846222-021c-5367-8296-b665ce9afeb9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65851/selection/07a3540ad51bfb53d362c69b0c3835b387a5d7d769d089dc5189f608ec57d640" :answer/id #uuid "48023e4b-c5e8-59e9-9dfb-6d957ec5e024" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65851/selection/8642f29c07ed588847b818ca52d7d9b13f60105c8ca35b3f5cb1a649a54ead1c" :answer/id #uuid "eb320fbd-d953-539a-9821-9e6d26e2001b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65851/selection/986e06f062dcc0ad37fbb185f7e0d56b0fd8e74b571035e7dc0af3d06af89951" :answer/id #uuid "0258d2dd-dda4-538a-a8f7-1450b914d022" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65851/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "64f888a9-fca8-58ba-be12-21695875f0dd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-65851/selection/8642f29c07ed588847b818ca52d7d9b13f60105c8ca35b3f5cb1a649a54ead1c" :answer-field/choices ["q-65851/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-65851/selection/8edf36f0d0c04b8e0e3f881a66fab0f1901a06368d5ca1f6d437f77714de6bc5" "q-65851/selection/07a3540ad51bfb53d362c69b0c3835b387a5d7d769d089dc5189f608ec57d640" "q-65851/selection/8642f29c07ed588847b818ca52d7d9b13f60105c8ca35b3f5cb1a649a54ead1c" "q-65851/selection/986e06f062dcc0ad37fbb185f7e0d56b0fd8e74b571035e7dc0af3d06af89951"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-65851" :question/id #uuid "c23519c0-b4cf-5df9-bbf3-a99ec81e76c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-65851" :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the exact solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})=1$ for $-2\\pi \\le x<2\\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "We will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2} & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the equation above for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2} & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{(4n+1)\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain $-2\\pi \\le x<2\\pi .$\n\n- Setting $n=-1$ gives $x=-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain $-2\\pi \\le x<2\\pi .$ So, the solutions are $x=-\\frac{3\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}+\\frac{\\pi }{2}=-\\pi .\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-65851/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9eb12a99-5169-52f7-8830-5de0d2d854f6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-65851"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-274701/field-1/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8" :answer/id #uuid "be6986a1-d2a7-5720-8d02-8ba1f861273a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-274701/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ebba82c0-7f08-53d4-a72b-d1667ec8a676" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-274701/field-1/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8" :answer-field/choices ["q-274701/field-1/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-274701/field-2/a59